{"event_type":"review","id":"32c091a50dbd938e09b57b6e523d34512ec94e293af67d4c00a4c67e22a988e8","occurred_at":"2026-11-16T23:29:20Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/45f1203c25915312547a5872ab73c471f54a35af408cd76264461204b8529dc7","sha256":"45f1203c25915312547a5872ab73c471f54a35af408cd76264461204b8529dc7"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/040e9b4929d59b6b1945e34dd28b6678cec08a525e921b833eb85517f17a1dd0","sha256":"040e9b4929d59b6b1945e34dd28b6678cec08a525e921b833eb85517f17a1dd0"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5316bc37f6db5121802354163d19e1e788ae14e06901738332ced37c76b9b973","sha256":"5316bc37f6db5121802354163d19e1e788ae14e06901738332ced37c76b9b973"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/633a1411bf9b13ed92a1f3e74e069eb4db9ae569650a6840a21664847dfafc16","sha256":"633a1411bf9b13ed92a1f3e74e069eb4db9ae569650a6840a21664847dfafc16"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a490211c1ac9fb9500ca0fbaf18bf7a7aa919cc108c2df48900fc2f756dc8bfe","sha256":"a490211c1ac9fb9500ca0fbaf18bf7a7aa919cc108c2df48900fc2f756dc8bfe"}],"attempt_id":"2886f2f2ad5ec554f80137db8ae0d303fb95beca169a8be3b21045ca9d88a7a9:0:1","base":"4909f2297fd2f752d35ba66cd46ac79297099bc5","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"3a26dc433e28fa9b0ffc22de16c1fba24db9ab43","body":"**Do not treat a superseded finding outcome as confirmed fixed.**\n\nIf another generation takes ownership after merge-head proof selection, `planRepairHarvest` returns `preserved-newer-generation`. At `src/ops/crq/internal/reconcileSourceFeedback.ts:102`, this function returns success without recording a fixed event.\n\nFor an ordinary merge-head proof, `publishSource` does not recheck canonical terminal truth. It can therefore resolve the source thread, and `reconcileFixRun` can record `fix_merged`, while the finding remains delivered to the newer job.\n\nPropagate the skipped outcome and defer feedback, or require current fixed evidence before source resolution. Preserve the supported threadless legacy path.","id":"a405d8ca0da0052260295d3fe13d07e3ffe4db893ef4618fba6302af0ea5ef7e","intervals":[[102,102]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/reconcileSourceFeedback.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Do not treat a superseded finding outcome as confirmed fixed."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"b6b3c460b23b71ac4a53599c6aad2f71af116fd1","body":"**Check item and run ownership in the canonical fixed-event path.**\n\n`canonicalFixedEvents` checks only the job ID and record membership for each FIXED job. It does not compare the job's `item` or `run` with the repair record. The merge-head path (`reconcileMergeProof.ts:189-196`) and `validateFixedEvidence` (`reconcileMergeProof.ts:100-106`) both reject those mismatches. A FIXED job that carries another item or run can therefore select canonical proof through this path, and no local guard rejects it before source feedback uses that proof.\n\nThe check is missing here, but the reachability of such a job depends on how repair records are written. The inspected writers do not show that a record can hold a foreign job. Treat the impact as hardening unless that write path is confirmed.\n\nAdd the owner fields to the canonical input and check them with the job identity:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n export interface CanonicalFixedEventsInput {\n+  /** Item and run that own the repair record. */\n+  readonly itemId: string;\n+  readonly run: string;\n   /** Job ids whose recorded verdict is FIXED, in record order. */\n   readonly fixedJobs: readonly string[];\n```\n\n```diff\n-    if (job.get('job') !== id || !input.recordJobs.includes(id))\n+    if (\n+      job.get('job') !== id ||\n+      job.get('item') !== input.itemId ||\n+      job.get('run') !== input.run ||\n+      !input.recordJobs.includes(id)\n+    )\n       throw new Error('canonical fixed repair job identity mismatch');\n```\n\nIn `canonicalProof`, pass the context through and supply the owner fields:\n\n```diff\n export async function canonicalProof(\n+  context: MergeProofContext,\n   record: JsonObject,\n   info: JsonObject,\n   effects: MergeProofEffects,\n ): Promise<JsonObject | null> {\n   const published = object(record.get('publication')).get('head');\n   const projection = await canonicalFixedEvents(\n     {\n+      itemId: context.itemId,\n+      run: context.run,\n       fixedJobs: fixedJobs(record),\n```\n\nUpdate both calls in `proveMerge` (lines 166 and 168) to pass `context`. Search for other `canonicalProof` callers before changing the signature.\n\n</details>","id":"80048f1029d308742ec02f0917384bba9f3ee7976796b07e01bb46f8b51eb04d","intervals":[[134,134]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/reconcileMergeProof.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Check item and run ownership in the canonical fixed-event path."}],"head":"0001eae94fb2642b2174752df19466dab212929f","head_tree":"2a6378f38614c8b16a7d30447cf71e2ddc2985f6","input_scope":[{"blob":"c2e30328d08fdac7626b29d8b00f8e4e9f0d4482","intervals":[[1,200]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/backfillHarvestCounted.ts"},{"blob":"10a4a9869d6c1258d772e387ee9d4c6b7bab918d","intervals":[[1,186]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/deliverPending.ts"},{"blob":"40ac1fc6c5eebc7cce3908fe1ff137fbb9de8091","intervals":[[1,281]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/deliverPrReviews.ts"},{"blob":"c2384badd5e7dc63e54314dbba87e120a067a8c2","intervals":[[1,178]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/deliverPushFindings.ts"},{"blob":"9aac504afe8c6c182a352e88397738eaa1cfd87d","intervals":[[1,188]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/deliverRefreshes.ts"},{"blob":"f800f243d3b44d100d911b8cb38e8cd4e1079734","intervals":[[1,195]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/rec